Honour send-lf on wwan AT ports instead of forcing the LF.

MM terminates AT commands with CRLF on every non-TTY subsystem, unconditionally.
The s5400's umts_router channel wants a bare CR: sent "AT\r\n" it echoes "AT\r"
and then never completes the command, because the LF is left sitting in its
parser and swallows the front of the next one. MM's probe therefore sends "AT"
five times, gets nothing back, concludes the port is not AT-capable, and the
plugin cannot grab it -- which leaves the modem with only a SIT port and MM
gives up with "modem is unusable".

Worse, one CRLF poisons the channel until the driver is unbound and rebound, so
this is not merely a probe-time nuisance.

send_lf defaults to FALSE, so wwan AT ports now get a bare CR like the CP wants.

diff --git a/src/mm-port-serial-at.c b/src/mm-port-serial-at.c
index ca2cc540..2af17ba5 100644
--- a/src/mm-port-serial-at.c
+++ b/src/mm-port-serial-at.c
@@ -354,15 +354,13 @@ mm_port_serial_at_command (MMPortSerialAt *self,
     g_return_if_fail (self != NULL);
     g_return_if_fail (MM_IS_PORT_SERIAL_AT (self));
     g_return_if_fail (command != NULL);
 
     buf = at_command_to_byte_array (command,
                                     is_raw,
-                                    (mm_port_get_subsys (MM_PORT (self)) == MM_PORT_SUBSYS_TTY ?
-                                     self->priv->send_lf :
-                                     TRUE));
+                                    self->priv->send_lf);
     g_return_if_fail (buf != NULL);
 
     task = g_task_new (self, NULL, callback, user_data);
 
     mm_port_serial_command (MM_PORT_SERIAL (self),
                             buf,
